  "behavior": [
    "An actual registered or funded decoder source is consumed only through the original fresh prompt claim and exact request funding account; direct and complete source health are checked under the same lock as the protected host hold.",
    "One dense buffer is filled without growth or conversion. Partial and completed errors retain source, original prompt claim and full host custody; native source pins and completion remain in a separate scope.",
    "Exact publication attaches the actual table charge before exposure, shifts D from reserved and protected bytes into registered payload with the original funding origin, and preserves total usage and peak. P-D retires only afterward.",
    "Shared and ordinary registry keys retain one K namespace without adding Sync to the existing ordinary Send-only APIs. Existing pin, register and funded adoption find the published key and do not charge it twice.",
    "An externally retained shared key prevents final provider-key destruction while table/account locks unwind. Both entry search and checked arithmetic precede commit; the real second-comparison panic leaves transfer counters unchanged and preserves conservative poison.",
    "Only exact publication creates the finish-only prompt remainder. Finishing then owned-input binding establish readiness through existing stages; no old request, receipt or quota is promoted."
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "The initial off-tree helper inserted an owned K after counter changes. Independent review identified provider comparison panic and key destruction under locks; that draft was never applied.",
    "The revised helper uses a precommit vacant-entry search with an externally retained Arc and was independently reviewed. The pinned Rust entry/node source confirms vacant insertion does not repeat key comparison, including node splits.",
    "Root tightened HostSlotStorageKey and publish documentation to require independent payload-free identity data, preventing a table-token-to-registration ownership cycle.",
    "All 13 new tests and the production implementation passed on the first compilation/validation attempt; no source correction or rerun was required."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "These are exact inline managed-host payload claims with existing descriptor, handle and allocator bookkeeping exclusions; they do not bound total process memory or arbitrary nested constructors.",
    "Complete-source and direct registered/funded source behavior is covered. The new helper retains inherited residual-source pins by composition, but that branch has no dedicated new behavioral fixture.",
    "Native arrays, RNG/pending input, executable origin binding, decoder installation, final controller and fresh step authority remain separate work. Funded generic restore/fork is not enabled.",
    "Hybrid/paged state, whole-controller/facade/capture/ingress payloads and the full resident/host/disk/distributed/media/speculation matrix remain unfinished.",
    "The new transfer panic guarantee does not broaden the pre-existing arbitrary-provider comparison contract of ordinary inventory insertion.",
    "No new released-checkpoint, distributed hardware or total-process peak-memory measurements were performed."
  ]
